[Answered on #75](https://github.com/asalzburger/nodd/pull/75#issuecomment-6163783411).

The 800 mm LAr gap is a provisional routing allowance. Si-W allocates services outside the ECAL and through a 400 mm rear gap; its 30 mm front seam is installation-only.

I clarified the overview and matching four-page PDF: :codex-file-citation{path="[redacted]" purpose="output"}. Proposed actions:

- :codex-followup[Define cryostat exits]{prompt="Define actual LAr service headers, feedthrough positions and connection envelopes."}
- :codex-followup[Compare alternative routes]{prompt="Compare front S-bends with side outlets and rear egress to determine whether the LAr front gap can shrink."}
- :codex-followup[Validate the transition]{prompt="After selecting a service route, validate the revised barrel/endcap transition and HCAL/FCal interfaces."}
